CASE WHEN convertedManaCost = 16 THEN 1 END) or SUM(CASE WHEN ... THEN 1 ELSE 0 END).\n\nActually, in SQLite, SUM(convertedManaCost = 16) works because boolean expressions evaluate to 0/1. But to be safe and clear, use SUM(CASE WHEN convertedManaCost = 16 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END).\n\nHmm, but wait \u2014 if convertedManaCost is NULL for some rows, convertedManaCost = 16 is NULL, and SUM ignores NULLs, so SUM(convertedManaCost = 16) would sum 0s and 1s over non-null rows \u2014 that's fine, equals count of rows where it equals 16.\n\nDenominator: COUNT(convertedManaCost) counts non-null convertedManaCost rows.\n\nSo the corrected query:\n\n```sql\nSELECT CAST(SUM(CASE WHEN convertedManaCost = 16 THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS REAL) * 100 / COUNT(convertedManaCost) AS percentage\nFROM cards\nWHERE setCode IN (SELECT setCode FROM cards WHERE name = 'Abyssal Horror');\n```\n\nWait, but should I keep the proposed query's structure and just change 10 \u2192 16 and COUNT(*) \u2192 COUNT(convertedManaCost)? Let me check the proposed query against each audit point:\n\n1. Predicate polarity and connectives: The hint defines percentage as DIVIDE(COUNT(convertedManaCost = 16), COUNT(convertedManaCost))*100. The proposed query uses convertedManaCost = 10 \u2014 mismatch with the authoritative hint. Also denominator COUNT(*) vs COUNT(convertedManaCost).\n\n2. Output shape: SELECT list contains just the percentage \u2014 fine. No ROUND \u2014 fine. One row \u2014 fine.\n\n3. Tables/columns exist: cards, setCode, name, convertedManaCost \u2014 these exist in the MTG cards schema. Fine.\n\nSo the correction: change 10 to 16 (per hint) and COUNT(*) to COUNT(convertedManaCost) (per hint).\n\nHmm, but wait. Let me reconsider the 10 vs 16 issue once more. The question explicitly"], "452713e4fcf4261d8ad5508a56cb16d36c5064e2": ["```sql\nSELECT DISTINCT purchaseUrls\nFROM cards\nWHERE promoTypes = 'bundle';\n```"], "01d54246e7a871ab48d84daf83b23e31cb1f28d2": ["```sql\nSELECT subtypes, supertypes\nFROM ca