 of the cards with a converted Mana Cost of 10 in set of Abyssal Horror?\"\n\nHmm, actually I now recall there IS a BIRD question with \"Abyssal Horror\". Let me think... \"Abyssal Horror\" \u2014 is it a set? In MTGJSON, sets have names like \"Mirage\", \"Visions\", etc. Hmm, but there might be a set... Actually no. Wait \u2014 could \"Abyssal Horror\" be a card, and \"set of Abyssal Horror\" means the set containing that card? The hint says \"set of Abyssal Horror refers to name = 'Abyssal Horror'\". If it were the card, the hint would say \"cards.name = 'Abyssal Horror'\". If it were the set, it would say \"sets.name = 'Abyssal Horror'\". The hint just says \"name = 'Abyssal Horror'\".\n\nHmm. In BIRD, hints are like \"set of Abyssal Horror refers to name = 'Abyssal Horror'\". This is ambiguous but typically in BIRD for this database, when they say \"in set of X\", they mean sets.name = X. But is there a set named \"Abyssal Horror\"? That seems unlikely for MTG.\n\nActually wait \u2014 maybe it's a card name and the set is derived. Let me think: \"Abyssal Horror\" is a card from Mirage (a 5/5 flying Horror). Its setCode would be 'MIR'. So \"set of Abyssal Horror\" = the set containing the card Abyssal Horror = Mirage.\n\nHmm, but the hint says \"name = 'Abyssal Horror'\" \u2014 if it referred to cards.name, then the query would be: find setCode of card named 'Abyssal Horror', then compute percentage of cards with CMC=10 in that set.\n\nAlternatively, if sets.name = 'A"], "2f291b5b38e7e426d0e6c8f7fc0852327c478a0e": ["- cards(flavorName, artist)\n- Filter: cards.flavorName = 'Battra, Dark Destroyer'\n- No joins needed."], "bf719f57ba6e5697256abf0c7f1dc336d87fb4c4": ["```sql\nSELECT name\nFROM cards\nWHERE name IN ('Serra Angel', 'Shrine Keeper')\nORDER BY convertedManaCost DESC\nLIMIT 1;\n```"], "b0ddbd7f010041732565153e6c4b0220ca1ad6b1": ["```sql\nSELECT artist FROM cards WHERE flavorName = 'Battra, Dark Destroyer';\n```"], "041dac4e5a9ed694f6520eb335ff39617f0c906